self-check failed: acceptance criteria not met or not reported: "Run `cargo test`. It passes, including new tests that run the auditor against a fake driver and check that it records a typed finding."; redacted report: {"summary":"Added the auditor role, modelled on the audience. `athena audit` runs a model through the same driver and read-only tools (Read, Grep, Glob, no commands). Its workspace holds BRIEF.md at HEAD and OUTCOMES.md, the last 40 commits that changed the code with records-only commits left out. The brief carries no acceptance criteria. The model returns a summary and findings, each with text and evidence. Athena validates and redacts them, then records one `athena.audit-report/1` record (`records/audit-reports/<YYYY-MM>/<id>.json`), the invocation and the role definition in a single records commit. A finding with no evidence, or an empty summary, is refused: no report is recorded, but the paid invocation is kept. The CLI prints the summary, the findings and the invocation path, or the report with `--json`. `athena status` shows the latest report.

`Role::Auditor` ("auditor") round-trips through `as_str` and `parse`. `AuditorOutput` and its schema, `auditor_system_prompt` and `BudgetSet::Auditor` are added. `Records` gains `audit_reports` and `auditor_runs`. The fake driver answers the auditor, and the test harness gets `auditor` and `seen_by_auditor` fields. Docs: CHANGELOG entry, `docs/records.md`, and an auditor section in `roles-and-ladder.md`. The prompt's protection is marked prose-only in the AUDITOR_PROMPT comment, the auditor.rs module docs, the design doc and the changelog.

`cargo test --locked` fails on one test, which this change didn't cause (see open_issues). All new tests pass, and fmt and clippy are clean.","files":["crates/athena-data/src/roles.rs","crates/athena-data/src/records.rs","crates/athena-core/src/auditor.rs","crates/athena-core/src/lib.rs","crates/athena-core/src/store.rs","crates/athena-core/src/status.rs","crates/athena-core/src/run_pin_tests.rs","crates/athena-agent/src/fake.rs","crates/athena-context/src/outputs.rs","crates/athena-context/src/lib.rs","crates/athena-cli/src/main.rs","crates/athena-cli/src/display.rs","crates/athena-cli/tests/common/mod.rs","crates/athena-cli/tests/retry.rs","crates/athena-cli/tests/auditor.rs","CHANGELOG.md","docs/records.md","docs/design/roles-and-ladder.md"],"checks_run":[{"command":"cargo fmt --all --check","result":"pass","note":null},{"command":"cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings","result":"pass","note":"Run after all code changes, before the CHANGELOG edit; no warnings."},{"command":"cargo test --locked","result":"fail","note":"Ran as `cargo test --locked -q --no-fail-fast`. One test fails: athena-cli tests/drain.rs `a_change_to_max_concurrency_alone_does_not_invalidate_a_reading`. It replaces "max_concurrency = 2" in the athena.toml text, but athena.toml says `max_concurrency = 1`. So `before` equals `after` and its first assertion, `assert_ne!(before, after)`, fails. I did not run it on the base commit to confirm, and this change does not touch athena.toml. Every other test passes, including the new ones in crates/athena-cli/tests/auditor.rs and the unit tests in roles.rs, records.rs, outputs.rs, lib.rs and auditor.rs."}],"criteria_check":[{"criterion":"Run `cargo test`. It passes, including new tests that run the auditor against a fake driver and check that it records a typed finding.","status":"unmet","evidence":"The new tests pass: crates/athena-cli/tests/auditor.rs `a_run_records_a_typed_finding_from_the_brief_and_not_from_a_jobs_criteria` and three others. Suite-wide, one test fails (see checks_run): tests/drain.rs `a_change_to_max_concurrency_alone_does_not_invalidate_a_reading`. It expects athena.toml to say `max_concurrency = 2` and it says 1. I can't edit athena.toml, and this change doesn't touch it."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo clippy --all-targets` and `cargo fmt --check`. Both are clean.","status":"met","evidence":"`cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` finished with no warnings. `cargo fmt --all --check` printed nothing."},{"criterion":"roles.rs defines an auditor role with a fixed prompt constant and a valid RoleDefinition. The prompt says to judge outcomes against BRIEF.md and the owner's goals rather than a job's own criteria, to look at real outcomes rather than records, and to cite evidence for each finding.","status":"met","evidence":"roles.rs has AUDITOR, AUDITOR_PROMPT and `auditor()`. Test `roles::tests::the_auditor_is_valid_and_judges_outcomes_against_the_brief_with_evidence` calls validate() and asserts the prompt contains "BRIEF.md", "owner's goals", "acceptance criteria", "real outcomes", "not at Athena's records" and "evidence". It passes."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo test`. A test shows the auditor's brief contains BRIEF.md and not the job's acceptance criteria. Another shows a finding with no evidence is rejected.","status":"met","evidence":"tests/auditor.rs `a_run_records_a_typed_finding...` asserts that what the fake auditor saw contains BRIEF-CANARY, the BRIEF.md text. It also asserts it contains none of the default reading's criterion texts and no "## Acceptance criteria". `a_finding_with_no_evidence_records_no_report` shows an empty-evidence finding (and an empty summary) is rejected and records no report. Unit tests in auditor.rs and records.rs cover the same. All pass."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo run -- audit --help`, or the equivalent test. The command exists and, with the fake driver, produces a recorded auditor invocation visible to the owner in CLI output.","status":"met","evidence":"`Command::Audit` is in main.rs. Test `the_audit_command_exists` runs `athena audit --help` and checks it succeeds and mentions BRIEF.md. The fake-driver test checks that `audited.invocation` ends with "-auditor.json" and that `Records.auditor_runs` has one Auditor invocation. The CLI prints "recorded invocation <path>". I did not run `athena audit` itself, because it needs a real or fake driver wired in through the binary."},{"criterion":"Role::Auditor has a name that round-trips through the parse and as_str functions in records.rs, and every exhaustive match on Role compiles.","status":"met","evidence":"The new test `records::tests::every_role_name_round_trips` loops over all six roles. Matches in fake.rs, run_pin_tests.rs and tests/retry.rs were updated; the whole workspace builds under clippy --all-targets."},{"criterion":"No warden code is added. The change does not edit BRIEF.md, athena.toml, defaults.toml, or any workflow file. CHANGELOG.md has an entry for the auditor.","status":"met","evidence":"No warden code was added. None of the four governed files was edited. CHANGELOG.md has a new first entry under Unreleased/Added. I also edited docs/records.md and crates/athena-core/src/run_pin_tests.rs, which are not in the deliverables list. The first records the new schema; the second needed the new match arm to compile."},{"criterion":"The change records that the auditor's prompt is protected from jobs only by being a fixed constant. The warden request will enforce protection. This is marked as prose-only in the docs or code comments.","status":"met","evidence":"The AUDITOR_PROMPT doc comment in roles.rs, the auditor.rs module docs, the "Prose-only protection" bullet in docs/design/roles-and-ladder.md and the CHANGELOG entry all say the protection is prose-only until the warden request enforces it."}],"open_issues":["`cargo test --locked` has one failure that this change doesn't cause: crates/athena-cli/tests/drain.rs `a_change_to_max_concurrency_alone_does_not_invalidate_a_reading`. It replaces "max_concurrency = 2" with "= 1" and "= 3" in the athena.toml text, but athena.toml says `max_concurrency = 1`. `before` and `after` come out the same and `assert_ne!(before, after)` fails. I did not run it on the base commit to confirm. Fixing it means editing athena.toml or that test, and the brief doesn't list athena.toml as a deliverable, so I left it.","The auditor's cadence (20 finished tasks) is a field only; nothing schedules it, as the request says.","The warden is not built, so the prompt's protection is prose-only."],"mistakes":["I first ran the whole `cargo test --locked` without `-q`. Its output was too large to read, so I reran it quietly to find the failure."],"learnings":["The audience is wired through many places: Role, AnyRecord (path, schema, validate), Records::load, BudgetSet, the fake driver, run_pin_tests.rs, the test harness in tests/common, tests/retry.rs, status and display.","athena-cli/tests/common/mod.rs builds test configs from the real athena.toml via include_str!. tests/drain.rs assumes `max_concurrency = 2` there, but the file says 1.","`Git::show_file(treeish, path)` returns Option<Vec<u8>>, and `Git::run` is used for `git log` with a pathspec exclude.","The producer's Bash hook rejects `tail`. Cargo output that is too large is saved outside the working directory, where Read and Grep can't open it. `cargo test -q --no-fail-fast` keeps output small enough to read."],"desires":["A way to read the saved output of a long cargo test run; it was written outside my working directory and Read and Grep refused it."]}
